WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:08.266
<v Audio Description>Visual scene one: Card one glows amber beside a 3D cyan polyhedron ringed by seven evenly spaced emerald yardstick nodes.

2
00:00:08.606 --> 00:00:15.736
<v Presenter>First, real compilers break any single descriptive rule, so this study defines a seven-part yardstick instead.

3
00:00:16.076 --> 00:00:24.565
<v Audio Description>Visual scene two: Card two turns cyan as tall rose upfront-power bars tower above short run-time bars on thirty percent of test workloads.

4
00:00:24.905 --> 00:00:32.518
<v Presenter>Second, maximum compiler optimization burns upfront energy that never pays back on thirty percent of test programs.

5
00:00:32.858 --> 00:00:42.104
<v Audio Description>Visual scene three: Card three locks in emerald as position-indexed cyan blocks snap into place, cutting warm Rust compile energy over four hundredfold.

6
00:00:42.444 --> 00:00:50.589
<v Presenter>Third, fingerprinting code by variable position reuses builds with zero mix-ups, cutting Rust compile energy four hundredfold.
